---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy | DALSAT"
  description="How DALSAT collects, uses and protects the personal data of anyone who gets in touch through the site."
  currentPath="/politica-privacidad"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  updated="2 September 2026"
  noindex={true}
  idioma="en"
>
  {/* PENDIENTE: igual que la version castellana. Al constituir la sociedad,
      poner razon social, NIF/CIF y domicilio del responsable del tratamiento,
      y quitar el parrafo de "en constitucion". */}
  <div>
    <h2>1. Who processes your data</h2>
    <p>
      The controller is the team trading as DALSAT. The company is in the process of being
      incorporated, so there is no registered name, tax number or registered address to publish yet.
      As soon as registration is complete, those details will appear here.
    </p>
    <p>
      For anything to do with your data, including exercising your rights, the channel is
      <a href="mailto:dalsat.soluciones@gmail.com">dalsat.soluciones@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Only what you give us. Through the contact form: your name or company, email, type of business
      and the message you write. If you write to us on WhatsApp, the data in that conversation stays
      with WhatsApp, whose controller is Meta and whose terms you accept by using it.
    </p>
    <p>
      In addition, if you accept the analytics cookies, we collect browsing data in aggregate and
      without identifying you. That is set out in the <a href="/en/cookies">cookie policy</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>3. What we use it for</h2>
    <p>
      To reply to you, to prepare a quote, and to provide the service if you end up hiring us. We do
      not sell your data and we do not add you to mailing lists unless you ask.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>4. On what legal basis</h2>
    <p>
      On your consent, given when you send the form or write to us, under Article 6(1)(a) of Regulation
      (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and Spanish Organic Law 3/2018 (LOPDGDD). If we go on to sign something, the
      basis becomes performance of the contract, under Article 6(1)(b).
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      For as long as there is a relationship or a commercial interest. After that, for as long as the
      law requires for tax and accounting obligations. If you ask us to delete it, we delete it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>6. Who else sees it</h2>
    <p>
      Nobody, other than the providers we need for the site and the email to work. They act as
      processors under Article 28 GDPR and may only use the data to provide their service to us:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Vercel Inc., website hosting and visit statistics.</li>
      <li>Formspree Inc., receiving the contact form messages.</li>
      <li>Google Ireland Ltd., email.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Some of these providers are in the United States. Where that is the case, the transfer relies on
      the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or on the European Commission's standard contractual clauses.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>7. What you can do</h2>
    <p>
      Ask us for access to your data, to correct it, to delete it, to stop processing it, to restrict
      its use, or to pass it to someone else. You ask by writing to
      <a href="mailto:dalsat.soluciones@gmail.com">dalsat.soluciones@gmail.com</a>. If you believe we
      have not handled it properly, you can complain to the Spanish Data Protection Agency at
      <a href="https://www.aepd.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.aepd.es</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>8. How we protect it</h2>
    <p>
      Data travels encrypted and is held in services with restricted access. We apply reasonable
      technical and organisational measures so that it is not lost and does not end up seen by anyone
      who should not see it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>9. Your customers' data when you are our customer</h2>
    <p>
      If you take on an agent, custom software or the panel, your customers' data passing through those
      tools remains yours. We are the processor and you are the controller. That is governed by the
      contract we sign, not by this page.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>10. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If the law changes or our services change, we update this page and the date at the top of it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Legal>
